    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The authors introduce a <strong>latent variable model</strong> that consists of a decoder function f, a transition model p, and a dependency graph G. The model is learned using a variational autoencoder (VAE) with a sparsity constraint on the graph. The <strong>entanglement map</strong> is used to describe the functional relationship between the learned and ground-truth representations.",
